# CODEOWNERS — review routing (plan FND-12).
#
# One human owns this repository, so the global rule is the substance and the
# specific rules below exist to make the *reason* for review explicit rather than
# to route to different people. When a second reviewer joins, these lines are
# where they get added.
#
# Note what CODEOWNERS cannot do: it requests review, it does not enforce it.
# The controls that actually block a bad change are the `dev` GitHub environment's
# required reviewer (terraform apply, helmfile apply) and the CI gates
# (contracts-check, ownership-check, trivy). See ADR-0010 and docs/review-policy.md.

# Everything, by default.
*                                   @canhtoanptit

# --- things that cost money or can destroy state -----------------------------
# Terraform is CI-apply-only and env-gated (ADR-0010); a review here is the last
# point at which a destroy-and-recreate is cheap to notice.
/infrastructure/terraform/          @canhtoanptit
/scripts/cost/                      @canhtoanptit
/scripts/dr/                        @canhtoanptit
/docs/cost-model.md                 @canhtoanptit
/docs/runbooks/                     @canhtoanptit

# --- things that change what runs in the cluster ------------------------------
/deployment/                        @canhtoanptit
/.github/workflows/                 @canhtoanptit
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @canhtoanptit

# --- frozen or governance-critical -------------------------------------------
# Released files under contracts/** are immutable after `contracts-v1.0`
# (CLAUDE.md §7); CI fails a PR that edits one, and this line makes the intent
# visible in the review UI as well.
/contracts/                         @canhtoanptit

# Ownership map and delegation conventions are lead-agent-only.
/docs/ownership.yaml                @canhtoanptit
/docs/implementation-plan.md         @canhtoanptit
/CLAUDE.md                          @canhtoanptit
